{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Do not send.</b> To slaughter. He said to Him: if so, for nothing did I come here — let me do him a wound and draw from him a little blood. He said to him: <b>do not do anything to him</b> — do not make in him a blemish." "<b>For now I know.</b> Rabbi Abba said: Abraham said to Him, let me set out before You my complaint: yesterday You said to me ״כִּי בְיִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ זָרַע״, and You turned and said ״קַח נָא אֶת בִּנְךָ״, now You say ״do not send your hand to the boy״? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: לֹא אֲחַלֵּל בְּרִיתִי וּמוֹצָא שְׂפָתַי לֹא אֲשַׁנֶּה (Psalms 89); when I said to you ״Take״ — מוֹצָא שְׂפָתַי לֹא אֲשַׁנֶּה — I did not say to you, slaughter him, but bring him up. I had you bring him up — now bring him down." "<b>For now I know.</b> From now on I have what to answer the adversary and the foolish nations — what is My love toward you; I have an opening of the mouth now, that they see that יְרֵא אֱלֹהִים אַתָּה."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:00.097359275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}